# Repo-root .dockerignore -- needed because agent/Dockerfile's build
# context is the repo root (not just agent/), so tools.py's Level 3 cloud
# reads can COPY in the sibling aeroflux/aeroflux_ml package. Without
# this, `docker build -f agent/Dockerfile .` sends the WHOLE repo as
# build context -- found doing exactly that locally (2026-08-14):
# aeroflux/data (34G) + aeroflux/bts_out (14G) + agent/.venv (6.2G) is
# 54GB+ of nothing the Dockerfile actually COPYs.
.git
aeroflux/data
aeroflux/bts_out
aeroflux/out
aeroflux/logs
aeroflux/model_outputs
aeroflux/notes
aeroflux/dataset.csv
aeroflux/dataset.jsonl
aeroflux/*.log
agent/.venv
agent/.env
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
notes
images
docs
.quarto
*.qmd
*.docx
*.pdf
